cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it with the metadata below."
type: software
title: "tsbench: a benchmark of language models on Tanabe-Sugano ligand-field tasks"
abstract: >-
  tsbench is a benchmark of language models on Tanabe-Sugano ligand-field tasks: fitting the ligand-field parameters
  Dq, B and C to absorption spectra, reading term diagrams and finding spin crossovers. Each task is run under three
  tool conditions: no tools, a code interpreter in a sandbox with a fixed Python stack, and the TanabeSugano MCP
  server. The repository contains the generated task set with its oracles and hashes, the run planner and runner,
  the scorer, the statistics, and the code that draws the figures and renders the report pages.
authors:
  - given-names: Anselm
    family-names: Hahn
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - Model Context Protocol
  - ligand-field theory
  - Tanabe-Sugano diagrams
